{"agent_id":"pp3g-Y2aY-build-459-lifecycle-manager-sh-extend-the-liveness","agent_seq":8,"timestamp":"2026-08-24T07:33:04.789584358Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"530a3c9d-4178-4476-a672-d18669283b43","comment_uuid":"17ce0366-ae63-42ed-aa2c-e027c31e3dd6","author":"pp3g-Y2aY-build-459-lifecycle-manager-sh-extend-the-liveness","content":"Result: scripts/lifecycle-manager.sh implemented (1344 lines, stdlib bash+python3, no new dependencies) — converts the liveness watchdog posture into a lifecycle manager per .design/lifecycle-manager-design.md.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION SUMMARY\n- Wrapper loop around agent-liveness.py v2 (six-class verdict matrix unchanged) at LIFECYCLE_INTERVAL=120s default; --once mode for single-cycle runs.\n- Per-verdict post-transition action sets: COMPLETED (kickoff cleanup --only <agent> --yes + deliverable branch/ahead/merged check + model-evidence staging row), FINISHED-UNMARKABLE (findings-exist check on working issue parsed from KICKOFF.md + operator force-sweep flag + evidence row), FAILED (worktree preserved for forensics + failure alert with log-tail evidence bundle + relaunch-with-backup-model recommendation), KILLED (immediate scoped cleanup + orphan verification + termination record with evidence chain), PARKED (resume_at recorded from retry-after parse or 60min default window; kill suppressed; simultaneous-parking alert at >=2 agents), FROZEN (last-200-line opencode.log tail + pane tail as sha256-hashed evidence bundle -> auto-kill via kickoff stop --force per operator-granted spiral authority #443 rev3 -> scoped cleanup -> termination record -> backup-model relaunch rec). STALE-SUSPECT gets one warning cycle then escalates to the FROZEN path.\n- Transition refinement: PARKED override when STALE/LIKELY-FROZEN/DEAD verdicts coincide with an AI_APICallError rate-limit signature in the agent's attributed log section; FAILED-vs-KILLED discrimination requires POSITIVE kill evidence (tmux pane_dead_status 143/137); everything else conservatively preserves. Attribution joins session-creation lines (message=created id=ses_... directory=<worktree>) to session tails, tolerant of quoted-command pollution in the shared log.\n- Wave-level: main HEAD change detection -> rev-list origin/main..main count > threshold (default 5) -> copy-paste-ready push suggestion comment (#451 pattern); doctrine/knowledge content-hash snapshot (.crosslink/knowledge + docs/methodology + docs/standards + root canon) -> reverse-edge dependent lookup via frontmatter depends_on/related_documents/consumed_by -> DIS existence-validator on each dependent (built-in stdlib citation resolver; LIFECYCLE_DIS_VALIDATOR env delegates to the external DIS V1 script when it lands).\n- Safety: all mutations exclusively via crosslink CLI surfaces; state under /tmp/opencode/lifecycle-state/ (manager-state.json, events.jsonl, model-evidence-staging.jsonl, evidence/<agent>/, force-sweep-pending.txt); anti-loop = once-per-episode dedup per (agent,verdict), rolling-1h circuit breaker (default 24 mutating actions), consecutive-scan-failure cap halts the loop; LIFECYCLE_DRY_RUN=1 records every intended mutation without executing.\n\nTEST EVIDENCE\n- Harness at /tmp/opencode/lifecycle-tests/run-tests.sh: 46/46 PASS across 12 scenarios (T1-T12), including real-tmux kill-signature discrimination (exit 143 -> KILLED path, exit 1 -> FAILED path), retry-after absolute-timestamp parsing (09:30 UTC recovered exactly), parked-expiry reclassification to FROZEN, stale two-cycle escalation, breaker halt, fatal error-cap exit, vanished-agent reconciliation, and a fixture git repo exercising merge detection + push suggestion + dependent-doc DIS findings.\n- Six live DRY_RUN smoke cycles against the real 12-agent fleet: detected and correctly handled 5 real PARKED agents (Zen quota exhaustion signatures; kills suppressed; simultaneous-parking alert composed for #429), 1 real LIKELY-FROZEN agent (full termination chain dry-run: evidence bundle sha256-hashed, stop+cleanup recorded, termination record composed), 6 FINISHED-UNMARKABLE reviewers (findings-on-issue checks returned true booleans against live issues), 3 zombie-builder classifications, merge/doctrine baselines set. Second cycle on identical state re-fired zero actions (idempotent).\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED\n- Real (non-dry-run) execution of kickoff stop/cleanup and crosslink issue comments: never executed against live agents by design (orchestrator verifies; DRY_RUN gates all mutations). The CLI invocations match verified help surfaces but end-to-end destructive behavior is unverified.\n- FROZEN auto-kill on a genuinely frozen production agent: observed only in DRY_RUN; the one live LIKELY-FROZEN case recovered before a real kill was warranted.\n- Long-duration loop behavior (days): breaker window rollover, state-file growth over ~thousands of cycles, and log-grep cost growth as opencode.log accumulates (currently ~173MB, ~0.1-2s per candidate probe) are extrapolated, not measured.\n- retry-after parsing against real header formats other than the three patterns implemented (absolute timestamp, seconds, daily-reset-at): tonight's Zen errors carry NO parseable value, so all live PARKED records used the 60min default window - correct but means the header-parse path is fixture-tested only.\n- External DIS validator delegation (LIFECYCLE_DIS_VALIDATOR): exercised only via the built-in validator; the contract (validator <repo_root> <doc>, nonzero exit = findings on stdout) awaits the real DIS V1 script.\n- Multi-instance concurrency: two lifecycle-manager processes sharing one state dir would race (single-writer assumed, no lockfile).","created_at":"2026-08-24T07:33:04.782898257Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:myMRlDrE2bc+L3PLgBPdLLTwolyU/0LzjEla7UurROg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgGY7n1/eQGHAmImTkI6/KAd1sveMz2gtzBcMuT6aO+eoAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAjibMyqOqdyRreXsf1IQj5Y2mL7a9Tq0jL9r1S5SBipBhGX+mUzFnJ5IojqjVRhx/Q4oVBlmbCW3Uwm4A4jzmAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:myMRlDrE2bc+L3PLgBPdLLTwolyU/0LzjEla7UurROg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgGY7n1/eQGHAmImTkI6/KAd1sveMz2gtzBcMuT6aO+eoAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPFor5t9VBqYnSUIXFf1Bz+EMI55KRRCJvSNbSuA2oSoWAII1X3a8Gnd5E81yqo3/f9VyPjWt61LDsHEIaVRWQA="}
